      "problem": "If $-6+z=-10$, then $z=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's rewrite the left-hand side so that the first term contains the variable.\n\n$$\nz-6=-10\n$$\n\nTo isolate $z$, we need to perform the *opposite* of subtracting $6$ from $z$, which is *adding* $6$ to $z.$ Remember to perform the same operation on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-6 & =-10 \\\\ z-6+6 & =-10+6 \\\\ z+0 & =-4 \\\\ z & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
